@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Review complete. `go vet` clean, new tests pass. No blockers.
+
+**Should-fix**
+
+1. **Autostart retry can kill a manually started run.** `deploy.go:204-219` — `sup.start` unconditionally replaces the active child (`stopLocked` at `supervisor.go:192`). If an autostart attempt fails and an operator starts a demo through the authed route during the backoff window (which can span minutes: up to three 60 s readiness timeouts + 2/4/8 s sleeps), the next retry silently kills that run and spawns its own. Cheap guard: before each retry, bail if `s.sup.status()` reports an active run — someone else won, autostart's job is done.
+
+2. **Admin token intake is argv-only.** `main.go:659` — `-admintoken` puts the secret in `/proc/*/cmdline` and forces it into the pod spec's `args` (visible to anyone with `kubectl describe`). K8s convention is a Secret via env/file. The deploy manifests are out of repo per the ADR, but the intake mechanism is in-repo; an env fallback (`DEMOSRV_ADMIN_TOKEN` when the flag is empty) is a few lines.
+
+**Nit**
+
+3. `deploy.go:172` — `subtle.ConstantTimeCompare` short-circuits on length mismatch, leaking token length via timing. Comparing SHA-256 digests of both sides removes it. Marginal for a high-entropy token.
+4. `deploy.go:171` — `CutPrefix(..., "Bearer ")` is case-sensitive; the RFC 7235 scheme is case-insensitive (`bearer` is legal). Fine for a single known client, worth knowing.
+5. `main.go:658` — `-wspublic` is advertised verbatim with no startup sanity check (e.g., parses and has a `ws`/`wss` scheme). A typo'd value serves a menu that looks healthy and a map that never connects — the exact failure mode `-nobuild`'s fail-loud stat check exists to prevent. A one-line `url.Parse` + scheme check at startup would match that philosophy.
+6. `main.go:739` — `hs.Addr` is now redundant (`hs.Serve(ln)` ignores it). Harmless.
+
+**Checked and clean**
+
+- Determinism: `time.Sleep`/backoff and `time.Now` are all demosrv orchestration, never in a sim path. No RNG or map-iteration concerns; `runNonce` discipline untouched.
+- Contract: no NATS subjects or payloads change. The HTTP surface change (401 on gated POSTs) is exactly what ADR-0020 records; every flag defaults to legacy behavior and the tests pin both the legacy ws advertisement and default-open POSTs.
+- Gate coverage is complete: all seven mutating POSTs wrapped, all GETs open, matching the ADR's enumerated set; the internal autostart path bypasses the gate by construction (direct `sup.start`), as documented.
+- `wsPublicURL` correctly affects only client-facing advertisement (`advertisedWsURL`, `wsClientURL`, `reg.WS`); the identity/port probes still dial the listen address (`wsDialURL`), so readiness is unaffected behind the LB.
+- `prebuiltBins` fail-loud check, bind-before-autostart ordering, and keep-serving exhaustion semantics all match the ADR and are tested, including the real-`childSpawner` exec path.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
