@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+Vet, tests, and `-race` all pass on the staged tree; every non-gated route in the full mux table is a GET, so the gated set is exactly the mutating surface as the ADR claims. Findings:
+
+**Blockers** — none.
+
+**Should-fix**
+
+1. `deploy.go:257` + `main.go` signal handler — the shutdown check and the spawn are not atomic, so the orphan-child race the shutdown channel exists to close is only narrowed, not closed. Sequence: autostart passes the top-of-loop `select` on `s.shutdown`; SIGTERM lands; the handler runs `close(srv.shutdown)`, `sup.stop()` (which resets `abortGen` to 0), `hs.Close()`; *then* `startIfIdle` takes `mu` with a fresh generation and spawns. `stop()`'s generation-stamp only aborts starts already in flight — a start that begins entirely after `stop()` returns is unprotected, and `main` returns as soon as `hs.Serve` does, killing the goroutine mid-`waitReady` and orphaning the engine child on the ws port. Fix shape: a `stopped` latch in the supervisor set by `stop()` and checked under the same `mu` hold in `startGuarded` (or re-check `s.shutdown` under `mu`). Window is small (top-of-loop check → lock acquisition), so defer-with-note is a defensible triage under the repo's bar — but this is the exact scenario the Fable-round-2 mitigation targets, worth finishing properly.
+
+**Nits**
+
+2. `ADR-0020-demosrv-public-deployment.md` (diff lines 137–142) — the "token gate sits at the mux, ungated by construction" consequence bullet appears twice; the second is a truncated duplicate of the first. Docs-only, but it reads like a merge artifact.
+
+3. `supervisor.go:182–190` — `errAlreadyActive` (comment + var) is inserted between `start`'s doc comment and `func start`, detaching the "start returns the LIVE run id…" contract note from the function it documents. Move the var above the comment block.
+
+**Questions**
+
+4. `deploy.go:200` — `resolveAdminToken` gives the flag priority but offers no way to force-open when `DEMOSRV_ADMIN_TOKEN` is set in the environment (empty flag falls back to env). Intentional fail-closed bias? Fine if so; just confirming it's a choice, since a stray env var in a dev shell silently turns the gate on.
+
+**Cleared after checking**: adminGate is constant-time on content with the length early-return explicitly accepted, no credential echo, `WWW-Authenticate` set; `-wspublic` is verbatim in both `advertisedWsURL` and `wsClientURL` with registry-payload and deep-link coverage; `startIfIdle`'s idle guard rides the same `mu` hold as the spawn (no check-then-act); listener binds before autostart; `prebuiltBins` rejects non-regular files; no NATS subject or payload changes (the unauthenticated-ws-plane go-live gate is properly recorded in the ADR rather than papered over); no determinism-relevant paths touched — all wall-clock use is demosrv orchestration, outside the sim. `main.go` imports were already sufficient (`net`, `net/url`, `time`); `go vet` and `go test -race ./cmd/demosrv/` are clean.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
