+The hard parts hold up: the idle guard and `closed` latch both sit under the same `mu` as the spawn (`supervisor.go:216-229`), the reaper now clears `s.active` only when its run is still current (`supervisor.go:260-265`), `shutdownFinal` mirrors `stop()`'s abortGen stamp-before-lock dance, and the listener binds before autostart fires (`main.go`, `net.Listen` before the goroutine). The gate covers exactly the seven mutating POSTs; `handleDemos` copies the registry before stamping `WS`, so no shared-write race. No NATS subject/payload change; the HTTP surface changes are ADR-0020'd, and the ADR correctly flags the unauthenticated ws plane as gating go-live, not this commit. No determinism surface touched.
+
+**Should-fix**
+1. `deploy.go:271-291` — `autostartDemo` treats `errSupervisorClosed` as a transient failure and keeps retrying/backing off. In production the closed `shutdown` channel catches it one iteration later so the cost is one wasted backoff sleep plus a misleading "retrying" log during shutdown; an `errors.Is(err, errSupervisorClosed)` early-return next to the `errAlreadyActive` check is two lines and makes the log truthful. Borderline nit; fix if touching the file anyway.
+
+**Nits**
+2. `deploy.go:219` — `strings.CutPrefix(..., "Bearer ")` is case-sensitive; RFC 7235 auth schemes are case-insensitive (`bearer x` gets 401). Fine while the only clients are your own tooling.
+3. `deploy.go:299-316` — `prebuiltBins` accepts any-of `0111`; a root-owned `0100` binary passes the check but fails exec for the demosrv user. The exec failure is loud at first start, which the check exists to avoid — but genuinely marginal.
+
+**Questions**
+4. `main.go:334-352` (routes) — the gate is per-route opt-in; a future mutating route added without `s.adminGate(...)` ships open, and `TestAdminTokenGate` enumerates today's seven paths so it won't catch the omission. A default-deny wrapper (gate every POST at the mux) would make it structural. Under the repo's "too early to need this" triage bar this is a legitimate defer — flagging so it's a recorded choice, not an oversight.
+5. ADR-0020 says deploy manifests live outside the repo; the ws-plane-auth go-live precondition therefore has no in-repo enforcement point. Presumably tracked in the deploy checklist — confirming that's deliberate.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
