+Reviewed the staged diff (ADR-0020: demosrv `-wspublic`/`-admintoken`/`-autostart`/`-nobuild`) plus the full working-tree `supervisor.go`, `main.go`, `replay.go` seams. `go vet` clean, `go test ./cmd/demosrv/` passes (4.4 s).
+
+## Findings
+
+**No blockers.** The concurrency design holds up under scrutiny:
+
+- The `closed`-latch double-check in `startGuarded` (supervisor.go:222,237) is sound under Go's seq-cst atomics: a start that passes the second `closed` check has its generation covered by `shutdownFinal`'s `abortGen` stamp (supervisor.go:339), and a start that completes readiness before the stamp lands is reaped by `shutdownFinal`'s `stopLocked` once it wins `mu`. No interleaving orphans a child.
+- The reaper now clearing `s.active` (supervisor.go:273) is safe for all other readers: `stopLocked` no-ops on nil (correct — child already reaped), `withActiveReplay` already checked `a.done`, and the `handleStart` supersede check reads the mirror.
+- Gate coverage is complete: all seven mutating POSTs are wrapped (main.go:344-356), 401 precedes the handler's 404 so unauthenticated probes can't enumerate demo/recording ids, and the internal autostart path bypasses the gate by construction.
+
+**Should-fix**
+1. `main.go:324-329` — the `server.shutdown` field comment says the channel is "closed by the signal handler BEFORE `sup.stop()`"; the handler now calls `sup.shutdownFinal()` (main.go:146). Stale reference to the mechanism this very diff replaced — cheap to fix before it misleads.
+
+**Nit**
+2. `deploy.go:219` — `strings.CutPrefix(..., "Bearer ")` is case-sensitive; RFC 7235 auth-schemes are case-insensitive (`bearer x` gets 401). Fine for an operator-token API; noting it so it reads as a choice.
+3. `deploy.go:199-204` — a K8s-Secret-sourced token with a trailing newline (classic `echo`-into-secret footgun) will 401 forever with no hint. A `strings.TrimSpace` on the env intake would kill the whole failure class; also plausibly "too early to need this" under your triage bar.
+
+**Question**
+4. `main.go:167-169` — if `hs.Serve` returns a real error (not `ErrServerClosed`), `log.Fatalf` exits without killing an active child (now more likely to exist, thanks to `-autostart`), orphaning an engine on the ws port. Pre-existing shape, narrow window post-successful-bind; flagging in case you want `sup.shutdownFinal()` before that Fatalf.
+5. Public-GET surface: `/api/status` exposes the child PID and `/api/demo/{id}/params` the scenario knobs to the internet. Consistent with ADR-0020's GETs-stay-public decision — confirm the PID leak is inside that intent.
+
+**Contract/ADR check:** no NATS subject or payload touched; the HTTP-surface and ws-advertisement changes are covered by ADR-0020, which also correctly flags the unauthenticated engine ws plane as a go-live gate rather than a this-commit issue. KB index and ADR table updated consistently. Determinism: nothing here touches sim paths; the only randomness (`runNonce`) is pre-existing and orchestration-only.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
