+## Blocker
+
+**B1. `-admintoken=` (explicitly supplied, empty) silently deploys the gate OPEN — contradicting the ADR, the flag help, and the feature's own motivating scenario.**
+`deploy.go:217` (`resolveAdminToken`), `main.go:61`, ADR-0020 lines 106–111.
+
+`resolveAdminToken` treats `flagVal == ""` as "flag not supplied" and falls through to the env; with the env also unset, startup succeeds with the mutating routes open. But `flag.String` cannot distinguish `-admintoken=` / `-admintoken "$TOK"` (with `$TOK` expanding empty under a shell-wrapped manifest) from the flag being absent — and that `$TOK`-expands-empty manifest is the exact scenario the fail-closed design cites (deploy_test.go:873, though the test uses `"  "` because `""` is uncatchable by the current code). The whitespace-only guard catches `"  "` but not the far more likely `""`. Three claims shipped in this commit are therefore false: the flag help ("a supplied-but-empty token fatals (fail closed)"), ADR-0020 ("ANY explicitly supplied token that trims to empty — flag or env … fails startup CLOSED"), and the resolveAdminToken doc comment.
+
+Fix is small: after `flag.Parse()`, use `flag.Visit` to record whether `admintoken` was explicitly set, and fail closed on set-but-empty. Alternatively (valid triage) narrow the ADR/help/comment text to "whitespace-only flag or set-but-empty env" — but code and docs must agree before this ADR ships in the same commit.
+
+## Should-fix
+
+None beyond B1.
+
+## Nits
+
+- **N1** `deploy.go:262` — `strings.CutPrefix(…, "Bearer ")` is case-sensitive, single-space. RFC 7235 makes the scheme case-insensitive (`bearer x` from some clients will 401). Fine for operator tooling; note only.
+- **N2** `main.go:79` — the `-wspublic` validator admits userinfo (`wss://user:pass@host`), which would then be advertised verbatim to every client. Verbatim-by-design, so at most add userinfo to the reject list alongside fragments.
+- **N3** `deploy_test.go:851` — `TestResolveAdminToken` hand-rolls env save/restore; `t.Setenv` is shorter and also guards against accidental `t.Parallel`.
+- **N4** `deploy_test.go:838` — `syscall.Mkfifo` is POSIX-only; fine for this repo's Linux targets, but this test won't build on Windows if that ever matters.
+
+## Questions
+
+- **Q1** ADR-0020's deployment precondition (the engine ws plane is unauthenticated and `-wspublic` exists to expose exactly that port) is correctly scoped as gating go-live, not this commit — confirm it's tracked somewhere that will actually block the deploy (the pending-ADR queue in `adrs.md` doesn't list the ADR-0006 auth amendment).
+
+## Verified clean
+
+- Concurrency: the `closed` latch ordering in `shutdownFinal` (`supervisor.go:347`) vs the double check in `startGuarded` (`supervisor.go:222,247`) is sound — a start either trips the latch or has its generation covered by the abort stamp; no orphan path found. The corpse-clearing idle guard (`supervisor.go:225-237`) can't deadlock with the reaper (`done` closes before the reaper takes `mu`).
+- `handleDemos` copies the registry before overriding `WS` (`main.go:416`) — no shared-state race with the new `-wspublic` path.
+- Gate coverage is complete: every POST route in `routes()` is wrapped, all GETs public, matching the ADR exactly.
+- Token hygiene: env-sourced token stripped from child env (`main.go:215`), constant-time compare with documented length-leak acceptance, no credential echo in 401s — all tested.
+- Determinism/contract: no engine-core, NATS-subject, or payload-schema changes; demosrv wall-clock use is ops-plane. ADR-0020 covers the HTTP-surface changes.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
