@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Reviewed the patch plus the shipped `supervisor.go`/`main.go` context. The shutdown latch (`closed` + double-check under mu + abortGen stamp ordering), the idle-guard corpse handling, fail-closed token intake, and env stripping all check out. No NATS subject or payload change; the new HTTP behavior (401 class, `ws` value semantics) is covered by ADR-0020. No determinism-relevant code touched (control plane only). No blockers.
+
+**Should-fix**
+
+1. `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:317-343` — an operator's authed `POST /api/demo/stop` that lands while an autostart attempt is mid-startup gets overridden. `stop()` stamps `abortGen`, the in-flight `startIfIdle` fails with the generic `"did not become ready: start aborted (stop requested)"` (supervisor.go:486/521), and `autostartDemo` treats that as transient — the next retry finds the supervisor idle and restarts the demo the operator just stopped. The loop is careful never to *replace* an operator's run but does un-do an operator's stop. The abort error is a plain `fmt.Errorf`, so autostart can't distinguish it; a sentinel (like `errAlreadyActive`/`errSupervisorClosed`) treated as terminal closes it. Window is small (boot-time, ≤4 attempts) — defer with a note if you'd rather not respin.
+
+**Nits**
+
+2. `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:265` — `CutPrefix(..., "Bearer ")` is case-sensitive and single-space only; RFC 7235 makes the scheme case-insensitive (`bearer x` gets 401). Operator-only clients make this acceptable; noting since it's an API surface.
+3. `engine/cmd/demosrv/main.go:83` — `-wspublic` validation rejects fragment/userinfo/empty-host but admits a query string and path, which will ride verbatim into the `ws=` deep-link param. Probably harmless (maybe even intended for path-routed LBs); confirm it's a choice.
+4. `engine/cmd/demosrv/main.go:1147` (diff) — on the `hs.Serve` error path, `log.Fatalf` skips the deferred `os.RemoveAll(binDir)`, leaking the pre-warm temp dir. Pre-existing pattern for all post-`MkdirTemp` fatals; not worth a respin.
+5. `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy_test.go:854` — `TestResolveAdminToken` hand-rolls env save/restore; `t.Setenv` does the same and additionally guards against accidental `t.Parallel()`.
+
+**Question**
+
+6. `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:260` — with the gate off (`adminToken == ""`), `adminGate` binds the raw handler at `routes()` time, so the gate can never be enabled at runtime; the struct comment documents this as load-bearing. Fine today — just confirm nothing planned (config reload, token rotation) assumes otherwise, since rotation currently means a pod restart.
+
+The ADR's own framing is right that the real exposure is the unauthenticated publish-capable ws plane behind `-wspublic`; the diff's startup warning and the go-live precondition note cover it — flagging only that go-live must not precede the broker-auth amendment.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
