+Reviewed the staged diff (ADR-0020: `-wspublic`, `-admintoken`, `-autostart`, `-nobuild`), plus the surrounding supervisor/main context in the working tree. `go vet` clean; package tests pass (4.4 s). Checked the shutdown-latch/abort-generation interleavings, the corpse-vs-idle guard, token-leak completeness across every `exec.Command` site, and the full route table for un-gated mutating handlers — all hold.
+
+## Findings
+
+**Blockers:** none.
+
+**Should-fix:** none. The two things I'd normally flag at this level — the unauthenticated publish-capable engine ws plane behind `-wspublic`, and the token-less viz menu 401-ing with the gate on — are both already recorded in the ADR as a go-live precondition and a deferred follow-up respectively (`docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0020-demosrv-public-deployment.md:133-172`), with a startup warning for the former (`engine/cmd/demosrv/main.go:190`). That matches the repo's triage bar.
+
+**Nits:**
+- `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:265` — `CutPrefix(..., "Bearer ")` is case-sensitive and single-space; RFC 7235 makes the scheme case-insensitive. Real clients (fetch, curl) send `Bearer`, so this only bites hand-rolled callers. Fine to leave.
+- `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy_test.go:884-927` — `TestResolveAdminToken` hand-rolls save/restore of the env var; `t.Setenv` does the same and additionally guards against a future `t.Parallel()`.
+- `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy_test.go:871` — `syscall.Mkfifo` makes the test unix-only; the package is already unix-bound (`syscall.SIGTERM`), so acceptable, but a `//go:build unix`-minded skip would be cleaner if this ever meets Windows CI.
+
+**Questions:**
+- `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:335-336` vs `supervisor.go:353-359` — if `shutdownFinal` stamps the abort while an autostart's `waitReady` is mid-poll and readiness happens to succeed before the next abort check, autostart logs "demo … is live" and the child is then immediately killed by `stopLocked`. Purely cosmetic log-truth in a dying process; confirm you're fine with it.
+- `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:279-283` — retry envelope is ~14 s total (2+4+8 s). A slow-releasing ws port after a pod reschedule that exceeds that leaves an idle-but-healthy pod (documented keep-serving semantics, and K8s liveness won't catch it since demosrv answers). If that turns out common in practice, the manifests' probe should hit `/api/status` semantics, not just the port — deployment-side note, nothing to change here.
+
+Notable positives (verified, not assumed): the latch/abort ordering in `startGuarded`'s double `closed` check (`supervisor.go:228,253`) is sound under every interleaving I could construct — the generation is always covered by the stamp or the latch trips; the reaper now clears `s.active` (`supervisor.go:289`), so the corpse-blocks-autostart case is closed; token stripping covers both `exec.Command` sites (engine children `main.go:246`, go-build `main.go:142`); the bind-before-announce/autostart reorder (`main.go:225`) fixes a pre-existing announce-before-bind lie. No NATS subject or payload changes; no determinism-relevant paths touched.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
