@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Vet clean, full package test suite passes (4.4s). Findings:
+
+## Blockers
+
+None. The concurrency claims in the comments check out against the code: `shutdownFinal`'s un-incremented stamp (`supervisor.go:365`) is covered by the `closed` latch being stored before the stamp and re-checked after generation allocation (`supervisor.go:257`); the reaper now clears `s.active` (`supervisor.go:293`) so `startIfIdle`'s corpse-window reap is consistent; `stripEnv` covers both engine children and the go-build pre-warm; the gate covers exactly the seven mutating POSTs. No NATS subject/payload touched; the ws-advertisement change is flag-gated and ADR-0020 documents it. No determinism exposure — all new time/RNG use is orchestration-side.
+
+## Questions
+
+1. **`supervisor.go:349` + `waitIdentity`/`waitPort` `<=` compare — intentional semantics widening?** The round-14 fix (`startGen+1` stamp, `<=` probe) means a *different* start that was already queued on `mu` when `stop()` stamped now allocates `gen == stamp` and gets aborted too — the old code explicitly protected that start ("no stale-flag abort of an unrelated spawn"). Concretely: start-A in its readiness wait, operator clicks start-B (queues on mu), then stop — B now dies with `errStartAborted`, and if B were an autostart retry it gives up terminally. "Stop kills everything that began before it" is a defensible — arguably better — semantic, and the comment at `supervisor.go:346-348` scopes the guarantee to starts beginning *after* stop completes, so I read this as intended. Confirm and move on.
+
+## Nits
+
+2. **`deploy.go:268`** — `CutPrefix(..., "Bearer ")` is case-sensitive; RFC 7235 auth-schemes are case-insensitive (`bearer x` gets 401). Every real client sends `Bearer`, so fine to ignore.
+3. **`main.go:1024-1045` (patch lines)** — the `-wspublic` URL validation is inline in `main()` behind `log.Fatalf`, unlike `resolveAdminToken`/`prebuiltBins` which were extracted and tested. A `validateWsPublic(string) error` would make the port/fragment/userinfo rules testable; right now the most intricate validation in the change has zero test coverage.
+4. **`deploy_test.go:887`** — `TestResolveAdminToken` hand-rolls save/restore of the env var; `t.Setenv` does this and additionally guards against accidental `t.Parallel()`.
+5. **`main.go:1160`** — `ReadHeaderTimeout` doesn't bound request-body reads (the ctl `speed`/`seek` proxies read bodies), so slow-loris via body remains. ADR-0020 already defers abuse handling to the LB, so this is consistent — just noting the timeout covers less than "slow-loris clients must not hold connections" suggests.
+
+The ADR's own framing of the big one — the advertised engine ws plane being publish-capable and unauthenticated — as a go-live precondition rather than a commit blocker is the right call, and it's loudly logged at startup.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
