+- **should-fix** `engine/cmd/demosrv/supervisor.go:251` — A start already queued on `mu` can acquire it after `stop()` bumps `stopEpoch` but before the stopping goroutine acquires the lock. That start snapshots the new epoch and is therefore not aborted; `stop()` can then wait through the full 660-second readiness timeout before killing it, or the queued start can run after the stop completes. Track a pending stop or snapshot the epoch before queueing so a stop cannot be bypassed by pre-existing waiters. Add a concurrent queued-start/stop test; `TestAutostartStopIsTerminal` only injects the sentinel and does not exercise this interleaving.
