+Review complete. I read the full staged diff, the resulting `supervisor.go`/`main.go`/`replay.go`, the viz `config.ts` `ws=` consumer, and verified the staged tree: `go vet` clean, `go test ./cmd/demosrv -count=1` passes (3.8s).
+
+## Findings
+
+**Blockers:** none.
+
+**Should-fix**
+
+1. `docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0020-demosrv-public-deployment.md:172-174` — the recorded crash-recovery mitigation for one-shot `-autostart` ("crash recovery is the manifests' job — K8s liveness/pod restart") cannot fire as stated: when the engine child dies after a successful autostart, demosrv itself keeps answering every GET with 200, so any ordinary HTTP liveness probe on demosrv never fails and the pod is never restarted — the demo stays down until a human intervenes. The ADR should name a probe that actually detects the condition (e.g. `/api/status` body showing idle while `-autostart` was configured, or a TCP probe of the engine ws port), or demosrv should grow a health endpoint reflecting "autostarted demo expected but not running". ADR-text fix only; no code change required in this commit.
+
+**Nits**
+
+2. `engine/cmd/demosrv/supervisor.go:251` — a start racing `shutdownFinal` in the window between its `stopPending.Add(1)` and its mu acquisition is refused as `errStartAborted` (surfaced as 409 "stop requested") instead of `errSupervisorClosed` (502). Cosmetic status-code mislabel, shutdown-only window.
+3. `engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy_test.go:1060-1067` — `TestResolveAdminToken` hand-rolls env save/restore; `t.Setenv` does this and additionally guards against accidental `t.Parallel`.
+4. `docs/kb/INDEX.md:113-116` — the footer gains a "ratified" line for ADR-0020 but the newly added ADR-0019 checklist entry gets none, while 0016–0018 each have one. Docs consistency only.
+
+**Questions** — none open. Points I checked and consider settled: the viz reads `?ws=` verbatim (`viz/src/config.ts:50`), so a `wss://…` `-wspublic` value survives the client side; the constant-time compare's length early-exit and the header-only (`ReadHeaderTimeout` without `ReadTimeout`) hardening are both explicitly documented as accepted trade-offs; the 409-on-stop-pending semantic change and the new 401 surface are covered by ADR-0020; no NATS subject or payload changes anywhere in the diff, and nothing touches the deterministic kernel (no map iteration, float accumulation, wall-clock, or RNG in sampled paths — all new time/backoff use is orchestration-side).
+
+The `stopEpoch`/`stopPending`/`closed` interleaving in `startGuarded` is sound as far as I can trace it: every stop either trips the pending refusal, invalidates the epoch snapshot (probe abort or final revalidation), or hits the double-checked closed latch, and the reaper now clearing `s.active` under mu is consistent with `stopLocked` (nil-safe) and `withActiveReplay` (done-channel check).
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
