@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+**Verdict: no blockers.** The concurrency redesign (epoch/pending/closed replacing startGen/abortGen) traces correct under every interleaving I checked: stop's pending→epoch order vs. startGuarded's epoch-snapshot→pending-check order closes the gap both directions, the final revalidation under mu catches stops marked during readiness, and the reaper/idle-guard interplay (`s.active = nil` in both, guarded by `s.active == a`) can't clobber a successor run. Route audit confirms the gated set is exactly the mutating POSTs (`main.go:396-424` — no ungated mutating surface). No engine-kernel files touched, so no determinism exposure; wall-clock use (backoff, `time.After`) is orchestration-side only. No NATS subject/payload changes; the `/api/demos` `ws` semantic change and the start-vs-queued-stop 409 semantic change are both covered by ADR-0020, and the broker-auth go-live gap is properly escalated to the pending-ADR queue. Sandbox denied running `go test`, so findings are static-analysis only — run the package tests before commit if not already green.
+
+## Should-fix
+
+None.
+
+## Nits
+
+1. **`engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:452`** — `prebuiltBins` accepts any execute bit (`mode&0o111`), not executability *by demosrv's uid*. A root-owned `0o700` binary in a nonroot pod passes startup validation and fails at first spawn — the exact late failure the check exists to prevent. `syscall.Access(p, unix.X_OK)`-style check would close it (stdlib `golang.org/x/sys` constraint noted; `syscall.Access` with `0x1` works). Container images rarely hit this; nit.
+2. **`engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy.go:300-313`** — `validateWsPublic` doesn't `TrimSpace`, and since the value is deliberately never echoed (main.go round-29 comment), a trailing-whitespace/newline in a manifest arg fails with the fully generic "not an absolute ws:// or wss:// URL" — hard to debug blind. Either trim (consistent with the token intake's newline-footgun handling) or distinguish the error reason class (still without echoing the value).
+3. **`engine/cmd/demosrv/supervisor.go:330` + `main.go:490-495`** — the deliberate-refusal 409 body reads `"<id> did not become ready: start aborted (stop requested)"` when the epoch abort fires inside `waitReady` — misleading phrasing for a refusal that isn't a readiness failure. `errors.Is` works, so cosmetic only.
+4. **`engine/cmd/demosrv/deploy_test.go:1085-1127`** — `TestResolveAdminToken` mutates process env, quietly barring `t.Parallel` package-wide later. Consistent with the package's existing global-var pinning style; fine for now.
+
+## Questions
+
+1. **`deploy.go:346`** — `autostartAttempts = 4` with 2s-doubling backoff gives ~14s total. A pod rescheduled onto a node where the ws port lingers in TIME_WAIT longer than that exhausts retries and sits idle until manual intervention (per the keep-serving design). Is the window deliberately this tight, or worth one more doubling? Manifests-side restart policy may cover it — committer's call.
+2. **ADR-0020:199** documents the token-less viz UI as view-only under `-admintoken`, but `-autostart` + a post-success crash leaves a public pod idle with *no* path back to running except an operator with the token. Confirm the manifests workstream owns that runbook (the ADR gestures at it; just flagging it's load-bearing for an "always-on" demo).
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
