+   numLanes / priority / oneway / width / allow / disallow / discard value
+   altered, added, or MISSING relative to stock? A type present in stock but
+   absent here silently falls back to netconvert's default for that class,
+   which would be a topology change smuggled in as a speed change.
+
+2. "The A/B on chi-loop shows identical drivable topology, and the -118
+   internal lanes / -102 yield approaches are an expected consequence of
+   lower approach speeds." Is that explanation actually right, or is it
+   post-hoc? Is there a reading where losing 118 internal lanes and 116
+   connections is a real defect?
