+  - NYC omission: `manhattan-grid` is in the tree; NYC's citywide default has been 25 mph since 2014 — same 5-mph-fast class as CA, undisclosed alongside it.
+  - Freeway approximation undisclosed: motorway 55 mph leaves CA freeway-corridor networks (`i280-woodside`, `merge-101-380`, `macarthur-maze`; 65 mph typical) 10 mph slow where unposted; only the urban-street approximation is admitted.
+  - `"${TYPE_ARGS[@]}"` on an empty array under `set -u` fails on bash 3.2 (macOS); fine on bash ≥4.4. The pinned Linux venv makes this theoretical.
+  - Provenance string names no typemap — a custom `TYPEMAP=` import shows only the REPO_REV hash, not which map. Cosmetic.
+
+  ## Questions
+
+  None beyond should-fix 4. Blockers: none — the mechanism, the A/B topology claim, the hash wiring, and the pass-2 reasoning all check out; the should-fixes are documentation accuracy in the ADR/typemap header, which matters here precisely because the ADR's evidence section is what future re-imports will be judged against.
+
+  REVIEW-COMPLETE
+
