+All checks done. Here's the review.
+
+## External review — deploy manifests for demosrv public deployment (ADR-0020)
+
+Verified against committed engine code: demosrv flags (`-wspublic/-admintoken/-autostart/-nobuild/-netcache/-overlaydir`) all exist (`engine/cmd/demosrv/main.go:54-63`), `DEMOSRV_ADMIN_TOKEN` env intake and child-env stripping are real (`main.go:142,246`), routes in README match the mux (`/api/status`, `POST /api/demo/{id}/start`), registry schema accepts every field used in `demos.public.json` (incl. `capacity`), run ids are valid tokens not ending in `-replay`, and `ticks: 3600` matches `sf-lean/scenario.yaml`. No NATS subject/payload changes; ADR-0020 amended in-diff to record the manifests' new home. No determinism-relevant code touched; seeds pinned. Go-live preconditions (unauthenticated ws plane, missing `/healthz`) are loudly documented in three places — good.
+
+### Should-fix
+
+1. **`deploy/k8s/ingress.yaml:32` — FrontendConfig annotation key is likely wrong case.** GKE's documented key is `networking.gke.io/v1beta1.FrontendConfig` (capital F, C); annotation keys are exact-match, so the lowercase `networking.gke.io/v1beta1.frontendconfig` would be silently ignored — no HTTPS redirect, no error anywhere. Verify against current GKE docs and fix before the eventual apply; silent-no-op is the worst failure mode for a security-adjacent redirect.
+
+2. **`deploy/k8s/service.yaml:7` — BackendConfig attachment depends on NEG backends, which is implicit.** `cloud.google.com/backend-config` (and its custom health checks + the load-bearing 86400s ws timeout) only takes effect with container-native LB. That's the default only on VPC-native clusters; if `carbon-dev` predates that default, the Ingress falls back to instance groups, the BackendConfig health-check ports (container ports 8900/8443) are wrong, and the 30s default timeout severs websockets — exactly what this file exists to prevent. Add `cloud.google.com/neg: '{"ingress": true}'` explicitly so the assumption is stated, not inherited.
+
+### Question
+
+3. **`deploy/demos.public.json` — all-or-nothing startup coupling to bucket contents.** `registry.Load` stat-checks every `scenarioDir` at startup (`registry.go:207-214`), so if any one of the six `<city>-lean` prefixes is missing from `gs://roaring-bots-traffic-sim/scenarios/`, demosrv fatals and the pod crash-loops — one missing city takes down the whole site rather than dropping one menu entry. Similarly, `deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:37`: `gcloud storage cp "gs://…/netcache/*"` errors on an empty prefix and fails the initContainer. Confirm all six cities + a non-empty netcache are uploaded; consider noting the failure mode in deploy/README.md.
+
+### Nits
+
+4. `deploy/demos.public.json:6` (and the other five blurbs) — parenthesis placement is garbled, and this is user-visible menu copy: `"(33.70,-118.75 → 34.35,-117.60. 1.38M lanes, the sprawl is the story.)"` closes the paren after the prose instead of after the bbox.
+5. `deploy/k8s/ingress.yaml:33` — `kubernetes.io/ingress.class` is deprecated in favor of `spec.ingressClassName: gce`; still honored today.
+6. `deploy/README.md:111-112` — step 2 is labeled "once" but the `--dry-run | kubectl apply` idiom silently rotates the token on every re-run, invalidating the operator's saved copy. Either drop the `apply` idiom or note the rotation behavior.
+7. `deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:326` — initContainer has no resource requests; fine on GKE Standard, would need them on Autopilot.
+
+No blockers. The only manifest-correctness risks (findings 1–2) are silent-no-op annotation issues that won't surface until the gated Ingress apply, which is exactly when nobody will be looking for them — worth fixing now while the file is open.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
