+Review complete. This is a deploy-manifests-only change (no engine/contract code in the diff); I verified the manifests' assumptions against the demosrv code that shipped in the previous commit.
+
+## Findings
+
+**Should-fix**
+
+1. **`deploy/k8s/cronjob.yaml:69-75` — `resources:` block is mis-indented to pod-spec level, not inside the `kubectl` container.** Parsed the YAML to confirm: `template.spec` keys are `[containers, resources, restartPolicy, serviceAccountName]` and the container has no `resources`. On clusters without the PodLevelResources feature (< 1.34), `kubectl apply` with default strict field validation rejects the CronJob and the README's piped apply exits non-zero; on ≥ 1.34 it is silently accepted as pod-level resources (semantically near-equivalent for a single-container pod, but unintended). Indent under `- name: kubectl`.
+
+**Nit**
+
+2. **`deploy/k8s/ingress.yaml:55-62` — "belt-and-suspenders" comment has it backwards.** GKE never creates an IngressClass object named `gce`; the GKE controller keys off the `kubernetes.io/ingress.class` annotation, and `spec.ingressClassName: gce` references a nonexistent object. Harmless as written (annotation wins), but the annotation is the load-bearing one, not the fallback.
+3. **`deploy/k8s/cronjob.yaml:389` — `kubectl:v1.35.5` version skew.** kubectl's supported skew is ±1 minor from the API server; `rollout restart` is a bare PATCH so it will almost certainly work regardless, but pinning near the cluster version is cheaper than finding out.
+
+**Verified clean (assumptions the manifests hardcode, checked against code)**
+
+- Entrypoint flags all exist with the assumed shapes: `-nobuild` is a **string** flag taking a directory (not a bool — the `-nobuild /opt/bin` argv parses correctly), `-wspublic` requires an admin token, and `DEMOSRV_ADMIN_TOKEN` env fallback exists (`engine/cmd/demosrv/main.go:54-63`, `deploy.go:31`).
+- `demos.public.json` matches the registry schema exactly (`registry.go:30-38`); `seed`/`ticks`/`capacity` are `*uint64`, values valid.
+- `scenarioDir` relative paths resolve via `filepath.Abs` against CWD (`registry.go:210`), so the Dockerfile's `WORKDIR /` + initContainer `/data` layout is correct.
+- `/api/status` exists and is an ungated GET (`main.go:402`), so probes/BackendConfig paths are real; mutating routes are all `adminGate`d.
+- `-overlaydir` tolerates a missing dir (flag doc confirms 404-by-design, matching the README claim).
+- Go 1.25 image matches `go.mod`; viz has no `packageManager` field so the corepack pnpm pin governs; viz build references nothing outside `viz/`.
+- CronJob cadence claim holds: serve defaults to `-pace 1` (real-time, `cmd/serve/main.go:58`), so 360k ticks ≈ 10 wall-hours > 6 h restart interval.
+- Contract discipline: no NATS subject/payload changes; both go-live preconditions (broker auth, ws `/healthz`) are consistently documented across ADR-0020, README, backendconfig, and ingress, and the ingress is correctly excluded from the deploy loop until they land.
