+Deploy-only diff (Docker + K8s + registry + ADR-0020 amendment). No engine code, no NATS subject/payload changes, so no determinism or contract exposure. I verified the manifests against the actual demosrv code: all nine flags exist (`engine/cmd/demosrv/main.go:54-63`), `DEMOSRV_ADMIN_TOKEN` env intake is real (`deploy.go:31`) with the fail-closed `-wspublic`-without-token fatal; `-nobuild` correctly skips `findEngineDir` so the module-less container CWD `/` is fine; registry fields in `demos.public.json` match `registry.go:30-38` exactly (run tokens valid, no `-replay` suffix, unique ids); the repo-root-relative `data/scenarios/*` paths resolve from `WORKDIR /` onto the initContainer's `/data`; the netcache is flat `<id>.v2.<hash>.geojson` files keyed by the same ids as the registry, so the non-recursive wildcard copy is correct.
+
+## Findings
+
+**BLOCKER**
+
+1. `deploy/k8s/cronjob.yaml:70` — the `resources:` block is indented as a sibling of `containers:` (pod-spec level), not inside the `kubectl` container. Outcome depends on cluster version: on <1.32 the apply in README step 3 fails strict server-side validation (`unknown field spec.jobTemplate.spec.template.spec.resources`), breaking the documented deploy pipe; on ≥1.32 the field parses as pod-level resources — either silently dropped (feature gate off) or applied with unintended semantics. Either way the container requests/limits you wrote never take effect as written. Two-space fix: nest it under the container entry.
+
+**SHOULD-FIX**
+
+2. `deploy/k8s/ingress.yaml:22` — `networking.gke.io/v1beta1.FrontendConfig: https-redirect` references a FrontendConfig that is defined nowhere in the diff or repo. FrontendConfig is namespaced and `traffic-sim` is created fresh here, so the object cannot pre-exist; the ingress will sync with errors and the HTTP→HTTPS redirect will silently not happen (plain-HTTP `app.phantomjam.com` serves the app, including the token in any operator's pasted curl). Add a `FrontendConfig` with `redirectToHttps: {enabled: true}` next to the ManagedCertificate, or drop the annotation. Go-live-gated file, but the manifest is incomplete as staged.
+
+**NIT**
+
+3. `deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:449-451` (initContainer script) — `gcloud storage cp` is overwrite-only; on an init-retry within one pod's life, objects deleted from the bucket linger on the emptyDir. `gcloud storage rsync -r` is the idempotent form. Bounded by pod lifetime; fine to defer.
+4. `deploy/README.md:130` — step 4 pipes `ingress.yaml` through the `:TAG` sed although it contains no `:TAG`. Harmless, but implies a coupling that doesn't exist; plain `kubectl apply -f` would document intent better.
+
+**QUESTION**
+
+5. `deploy/k8s/cronjob.yaml:64` — confirm `registry.k8s.io/kubectl:v1.35.5` actually exists (official upstream kubectl images are recent and tag coverage is spotty). A bad tag makes every restart Job ImagePullBackOff, and the failure mode it exists to prevent — site idle after the 10-sim-hour horizon — returns silently, since demosrv's `/api/status` keeps the probes green. Pre-launch, nobody is watching `failedJobsHistoryLimit`.
+
+Everything else checked out: entrypoint exec/`set -eu`/token-required-to-boot posture matches ADR-0020; non-root uid 1000 + fsGroup on the emptyDir is consistent for both gcloud (HOME=/tmp) and demosrv's `MkdirAll`; `.dockerignore`'s `viz/dist` exclusion prevents a stale-dist copy; Go 1.25 and the pnpm pin match `engine/go.mod` and the viz toolchain; the ADR-0020 amendment documenting the second go-live precondition is in the diff as required.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
