@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+You are reviewing a DESIGN SPEC (not a diff) in a traffic-simulation repo
+(deterministic Go engine, NATS contract, ADR-driven; project rules in
+AGENTS.md — determinism ADR-0005, message contract ADR-0006, contracts are
+sacred, stdlib-first Go, MapLibre-first vanilla-TS viz).
+
+The spec is the UNTRACKED new file docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0023-baked-replay-pipeline.md:
+a pipeline that bakes recorded runs (JetStream record plane, ADR-0006/0015)
+into static browser-replayable artifacts (PMTiles network, chunked quantized
+frame streams, lane-speed aggregates, an index.json) served from R2, plus a
+browser shim that mimics the live ws transport. It exists because the live ws
+plane is unauthenticated (ADR-0020 precondition) and cannot front the public
+site. NO code may be written — this is a design round.
+
+Read the spec first, then verify it against the repo: its file:line evidence
+(engine/cmd/replay/main.go, engine/natsio/player.go, frame.go, server.go,
+engine/geojson.go, viz/src/{nats-client,tssf,snapshots,main,replaypanel,
+congestion,netload,proj}.ts), its consistency with ADR-0006/0015/0016/0018/0020,
+and its size math. Also judge the design itself: TSRB/TSRL binary layouts,
+z11 region scheme, 60 s object-per-chunk layout, index.json schema, the
+shim's drop-in strategy (synthetic TSSF bytes + FetchLike stub for
+ReplayPanel), PMTiles/promoteId/feature-state feasibility in MapLibre GL 5.24,
+the tippecanoe choice, quantization choices, and the zoom-gating story.
+
+Report findings cited file:line, ranked: blocker / should-fix / nit /
